Whoah! The devteam were considering a mild -1 luck penalty, and even
commented that out until it could be balanced. You're considering huge
disadvantages, and then trying to balance them with huge advantages.

Elves taking an additional 1 pt. damage when hit with an iron weapon
is okay (or maybe just a random chance of extra damage--could be a
lethal difference at low levels). Taking damage just for touching iron
is too much. The devteam's idea of a luck penalty when wielding iron
would be fine.

Compensation, hmmm..... Perhaps a to-hit bonus and chance of increased
damage when wielding wooden weapons (includes all elvish, right?).
Maybe a +1 luck bonus when wearing elvish armor (or more elvish than
not, or elvish armor next to the skin--i.e., boots, helm, mithril
without hawaiian or T-shirt, or elvish cloak without anything beneath.
Benefit would be primarily early game; would lose the benefits when
choosing artifact weapons, scale mail, speed boots, special helms,
etc.
